# 4. TQS Form Section

The `TQS Form` is the primary information section.

This section will normally be completed before the shift and must capture the core Track Quality Pack and site information.

## Required behaviour

- Reproduce all relevant fields from the source worksheet.
- Preserve dropdown options and validation rules found in the workbook.
- Retain mandatory and optional field behaviour where it can be identified.
- Automatically save changes.
- Display clear validation messages.
- Make the form easy to complete on both desktop and mobile devices.
- Use appropriate controls for dates, times, numbers, selections, and longer text.
- Prevent accidental data loss.

## Shared data

Information entered into the TQS Form must automatically populate corresponding fields in:

- Site-specific sections
- TEF3071
- TEF3207
- Exports
- Any other workbook sections containing the same information

Use one shared underlying data model. Do not maintain duplicate, disconnected copies of the same value.

Examples of shared data may include:

- Track Quality Pack reference
- Project or work description
- Site name
- Site number
- Route
- Line
- ELR
- Mileage
- Track ID
- Date
- Shift
- Responsible person
- Other site or work details found in the workbook

Only implement mappings that can be identified from the supplied documents. Record uncertain mappings in the implementation plan.

