# 5. Photograph Capture and Management

The TQS Form must include a photograph management area suitable for site use.

## Required functions

Users must be able to:

- Take a photograph using a mobile device camera
- Select an existing image from the device
- Preview an image before saving
- Add a caption or description
- Associate a photograph with a site
- Associate a photograph with a pack section where applicable
- Record the capture date and time
- Reorder photographs
- Delete photographs with confirmation
- View photographs at full size
- Include selected photographs in PDF and Excel exports where supported

Use mobile camera-compatible file input settings such as `accept="image/*"` and camera capture hints where supported. Provide a normal file upload fallback for laptops, tablets, and browsers that do not support direct camera capture.

## Location information

When a photograph is captured on a device that supports location services:

1. Request location permission clearly.
2. Capture latitude, longitude, accuracy, date, and time.
3. Never prevent photo capture if location permission is refused or unavailable.
4. Store location information separately from the image file.
5. Display whether location was successfully recorded.
6. Do not expose raw location information to unauthorised users.

Review the Network Rail GIS repository available at:

https://github.com/openraildata/network-rail-gis

Use it only where its data, format, and licence allow reliable conversion of device coordinates into useful railway location information.

The application must continue to work when:

- Location permission is denied
- GPS is unavailable
- The GIS data cannot identify a railway position
- The device is temporarily offline

Do not assume the GIS repository exposes a live web API. Inspect it first and document the chosen integration approach.

