# 17. Authentication and Authorisation

Implement secure authentication appropriate for an Azure-hosted organisational application.

Keep authentication and authorisation isolated from the business logic so the identity provider can be configured for the deployment environment.

At minimum, support roles equivalent to:

- Contributor: create and edit packs
- Reviewer: review and update review status
- Administrator: manage configuration and archived records

Apply permissions on the server. Hiding a button in the interface is not sufficient authorisation.

Do not create default production passwords or commit test credentials.

